 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; The four resource budgets (P4 of the ADR, 2026-09-24). What a program
 ;; may DO is language; how much it may USE is the target profile. Every
 ;; profile below carries the same four keys, each with one :unit, one named
 ;; :trap and a per-run :default the embedder may override. A :default of nil
 ;; means NOT METERED on that profile (the key is present so the absence is a
 ;; stated fact, not an omission). Emergency stops (CPU / wall seconds) and a
 ;; host's own meters (kototama's Wasm-instruction counter) are named apart:
 ;; they are outside the semantics.
 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
 :budgets
 {:fuel   {:trap :budget/fuel   :means "function entries (a trampolined loop-helper re-entry is free on the reference / Wasm; the native backends charge counted self-recursion in bulk)"}
  :cells  {:trap :budget/cells  :means "heap nodes the run allocates: one per pair, kgraph datom, and constructed aggregate (variant, record, option/result, list, set, map, vector node), charged at construction so a shared value counts once. Native stores aggregates as pair chains, so a record of k fields is k cells there; a vector item is a cell of a second pool (the item arena) on native and is bounded per vector (:language/value :vector-items) elsewhere. Counts are per profile, not promised equal across profiles."}
  :bytes  {:trap :budget/bytes  :means "UTF-8 bytes of the strings a run produces (concat, substring, replace, case folds), cumulative; on native the string pool"}
  :frames {:trap :budget/frames :means "call depth; a self-tail loop is one frame"}
  :host-stack {:trap :host/stack-exhausted :why "Not a budget: the host ran out of its own stack before any budget answered. Named apart so it is never reported as fuel."}}

 :profile/reference
 {:why "osaho's KIR interpreter: the oracle every target is compared against at compile time. Set per run through kotoba.kir/execute :fuel :cells :bytes :frames."
  :fuel {:unit :function-entry :trap :budget/fuel
         :default {:value 512 :copies [{:repo "kotoba-lang/osaho" :path "src/kotoba/kir.cljk" :var kotoba.kir/default-fuel}]}
         :oracle-default {:value 100000
                          :why "The budget the compile-time oracle (kotoba.kir/lower) runs under when the caller names none; amu seals it as an unmetered native artifact's :limits :fuel so the verifier re-derives under the same number."
                          :copies [{:repo "kotoba-lang/osaho" :path "src/kotoba/kir.cljk" :var kotoba.kir/default-oracle-fuel}
                                   {:repo "kotoba-lang/amu" :path "src/kotoba/compiler/nbb/cli.cljk" :pattern "\\(def unmetered-oracle-fuel (\\d+)\\)"}]}
         :max {:value 9007199254740991 :why "2^53-1: the last budget from which every decrement to zero is exact on a JS Number."
               :copies [{:repo "kotoba-lang/osaho" :path "src/kotoba/kir.cljk" :var kotoba.kir/max-fuel}
                        {:repo "kotoba-lang/kotoba-verifier" :path "src/kotoba/verifier.cljk" :var kotoba.verifier/max-native-fuel}]}}
  :cells {:unit :cell :trap :budget/cells
          :default {:value nil :why "Not metered unless named (:cells n): this host never bounded aggregate nodes before P4, and a new default would stop programs that ran."}
          :pair-arena {:value 4096 :why "The interpreter's physical pair arena; exhausting it is :budget/cells {:arena :pairs} (was :heap-exhausted)."
                       :copies [{:repo "kotoba-lang/osaho" :path "src/kotoba/kir.cljk" :var kotoba.kir/default-pair-capacity}]}
          :kgraph-arena {:value 4096 :why "The kgraph datom arena; exhausting it is :budget/cells {:arena :kgraph} (was :kgraph-exhausted)."
                         :copies [{:repo "kotoba-lang/osaho" :path "src/kotoba/kir.cljk" :var kotoba.kir/default-kgraph-capacity}]}}
  :bytes {:unit :byte :trap :budget/bytes
          :default {:value nil :why "Not metered unless named (:bytes n), for the same reason as :cells."}}
  :frames {:unit :frame :trap :budget/frames
           :default {:value 32
                     :why "Interpreter call depth. 10,000 until P4, which was never reachable where this interpreter runs: under nbb/SCI each interpreted call is dozens of host frames. Measured 2026-09-24, fresh process per depth, non-tail (+ 1 (depth (- n 1))): kbb default stack 8 completes / 12 is :host/stack-exhausted; --stack-size=4096 (bin/amu, the corpus runner) 48 / 64, and with a 3-binding let 32 / 48. 32 lets the deterministic budget answer first on the compiler's host for those shapes; a smaller stack still runs out first, by its own name. Set per run with execute :frames."
                     :copies [{:repo "kotoba-lang/osaho" :path "src/kotoba/kir.cljk" :var kotoba.kir/default-frames}]}}}

 :profile/native
 {:why "A binary this machine runs under the POSIX kexe loader. The loader sandbox is defence in depth, not a language requirement. Every budget below is a per-run default the environment names (a packaged command bakes it)."
  :fuel {:unit :function-entry :trap :budget/fuel
         :default {:value nil
                   :metering :off
                   :why "ADR section 2: deterministic fuel is OFF by default on native (targets x86_64, aarch64 and their -linux / -macos names). The compiled charge still runs -- one decrement and one untaken branch per re-entering function entry -- against a counter the loader starts at 2^53-1, which no run reaches before the CPU emergency stop, and the report says :metered false. Measured 2026-09-24 on an M1 Max, fib(38) (126,491,972 charged entries): 0.26 s with the charge, 0.21 s with the charge compiled out, i.e. ~0.4 ns per entry; x86_64 under Rosetta 0.42 s vs 0.41 s. Opt in with KEXE_FUEL=n (packaged: --fuel n) or amu compile --fuel n: metered runs trap at the same count on both ISAs (recursive-list: 6,005 traps, 6,006 answers, aarch64 and x86_64)."
                   :override "KEXE_FUEL"}
         :unmetered-initial {:value 9007199254740991 :why "Where the counter starts when unmetered, and an unmetered artifact's :fuel-abi :initial."
                             :copies [{:repo "kotoba-lang/amu" :path "tools/kexe_loader.c" :pattern "#define KEXE_FUEL_MAX (\\d+)ull"}]}
         :max {:value 9007199254740991
               :why "Same 2^53-1 as the reference interpreter; a metered budget above it is refused."
               :copies [{:repo "kotoba-lang/amu" :path "tools/kexe_loader.c" :pattern "#define KEXE_FUEL_MAX (\\d+)ull"}]}
         :keeps-fuel-on {:why "Profiles where metering stays on by default, and why: aiueos kernel / user / UEFI objects (kotoba-native elf64 replenishes a per-call fuel tier per object and a per-interrupt tier at every ISR entry; elf64/artifact-fuel requires one sealed bound), the Windows loader (fixed 512, reads no KEXE_FUEL), android and ios (packaged by routes P4 did not change). amu nbb/cli unmetered-default-targets lists the unmetered ones."}}
  :cells {:unit :cell :trap :budget/cells
          :default {:value 4096 :override "KEXE_PAIRS" :why "The pair arena, where aggregates live as pair chains (aggregate ABI v8)."
                    :copies [{:repo "kotoba-lang/amu" :path "tools/kexe_loader.c" :pattern "#define KEXE_PAIR_CAPACITY (\\d+)u"}]}
          :pair-arena-max {:value 67108864 :why "64 Mi handles: address space, not memory."}
          :vectors {:value 4096 :why "Vector table entries: a second cell pool, exhaustion :budget/cells {:arena :vectors}."
                    :copies [{:repo "kotoba-lang/amu" :path "tools/kexe_loader.c" :pattern "#define KEXE_VECTOR_CAPACITY (\\d+)u"}]}
          :vector-items {:value 65536 :why "The item arena per run: one item = one cell of this pool; exhaustion :budget/cells {:arena :vector-items}." :copies [{:repo "kotoba-lang/amu" :path "tools/kexe_loader.c" :pattern "#define KEXE_VECTOR_ITEM_CAPACITY (\\d+)u"}]}}
  :bytes {:unit :byte :trap :budget/bytes
          :default {:value 65536 :override "KEXE_STRING_POOL" :copies [{:repo "kotoba-lang/amu" :path "tools/kexe_loader.c" :pattern "#define KEXE_STRING_POOL_BYTES (\\d+)u"}]}
          :max {:value 1073741824 :why "1 GiB of address space."}}
  :frames {:unit :frame :trap :budget/frames
           :default {:value nil :why "Not metered: the compiled code keeps no call-depth counter (adding one is a codegen change to both ISAs and a context ABI slot -- not done in P4). The guest stack is the host's (RLIMIT_STACK 1 MiB; macOS keeps the 8 MiB launch stack), and running off it is named :host/stack-exhausted by the loader's alternate-stack fault handler."}}
  :structural {:arena-scope-depth {:value 256 :why "Open arena-scope marks; a trap, not a budget of the four." :copies [{:repo "kotoba-lang/amu" :path "tools/kexe_loader.c" :pattern "#define KEXE_ARENA_SCOPE_DEPTH (\\d+)u"}]}}
  :emergency-stop {:why "Outside the semantics: an OS bound on the child, not a language budget."
                   :cpu-seconds {:value 1 :override "KEXE_CPU_SECONDS"}
                   :wall-seconds {:value 3 :override "KEXE_WALL_SECONDS"}}
  :static-elf
  {:why "The loader-less Linux static ELF targets, x86_64-linux-static and aarch64-linux-static (superproject adr-2609251400 C2, 2026-09-25). They run THIS profile: the cells and bytes budgets above are baked into the image at package time (the packaged-command case the profile's :why names), fuel metering is off by default exactly as above, and the trap names are the ones above. The packager, kotoba-native kotoba.native.linux-static, emits mechanism only (syscalls, register saves, the arena bump and range checks); which slots it answers, what an unanswered slot is called and what each outcome's exit status is are decided here and read by it."
   :admitted-slots {:value [:pair-new :pair-first :pair-second :string-equal :string-concat :string-substring :string-index-of :typed-cap-call]
                    :why "Context-ABI slots the prelude answers. Measured 2026-09-25 by scanning the emitted code of examples/recursive-list, recursive-tree and string-index-of on both ISAs: the pure programs reach pair-new and the v9 inline pair words, and the string one pair-new, string-substring and string-index-of; string-equal / string-concat / pair-first / pair-second complete the pair and string core. Every other slot of the artifact's context ABI is bound to a stub that traps :slot/unimplemented and names the slot. C3 (2026-09-25) adds :typed-cap-call, the capability slot: bound to the handlers below when the program has capability effects, and to its stub otherwise (nothing can reach it then). A slot listed here that the packager has no code for is a packaging refusal, not a stub."}
   :capability-handlers {:value {7 :clock/now 20 :process/spawn 23 :entropy/draw 33 :env/read 34 :fs/browse 35 :fs/app-data 37 :io/write 38 :cli/args 39 :io/write-error 41 :io/read}
                         :why "Capabilities (lang/capability-catalog.edn :compiler-wire-id -> name) whose handler the static image carries (superproject adr-2609251400 C3, 2026-09-25). The mechanism is machine code over raw Linux syscalls (write, read, openat2 with RESOLVE_BENEATH, fstat, getdents64, mkdirat, unlinkat, renameat2, clock_gettime, getcwd); every decision is amu-compiled Kotoba the image carries (amu tools/kexe_loader_decisions.kotoba, the kexe loader's own, and tools/linux_static_handlers.kotoba). :clock/now answers the text form only (\"wall\" / \"monotonic\"); :fs/app-data answers the read, write, exists, stat, mtime, mkdir, unlink, rmdir and rename forms, and since the second half of C3 (2026-09-25) append, range and chmod and the three proposed forms fsync, make-temp-dir and stat-nofollow (lang/capability-catalog.edn :fs/app-data :forms). The second half added :entropy/draw (getrandom, flags 0; ENOSYS is a named refusal, never a /dev/urandom fallback) and :process/spawn (clone / execve / wait4 over pipe2, dup3, close_range and PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS; the executables, bare-name lookup and passed variables sealed from the compile policy's :linux-static :spawn). A program whose effects include a capability not listed here is refused at packaging, by name."}
   :refused-capabilities {:value {}
                          :why "Capabilities refused at packaging BY NAME, so the refusal says what it refused. Empty since the second half of C3 (2026-09-25): process/spawn and entropy/draw, the two listed until then, have handlers. The kexe loader still answers both with the qualification host's identity stub, so the static image is the only native path that runs them."}
   :unimplemented-slot-trap :slot/unimplemented
   :exit-codes {:value {:ok 0 :trap/signal 120 :budget/fuel 122 :budget/cells 123 :budget/bytes 124 :slot/unimplemented 125 :capability/refused 126}
                :why "Process exit status per outcome. 120 is the kexe loader's status for a guest signal (SIGILL / SIGTRAP / SIGSEGV ...), kept so a caller reading either path sees the same code for the same trap; a budget or slot trap gets its own code because a loader-less process has no supervisor to name it after the fact. 121 is left to the loader's stdout-write failure. 126 (C3, second half) is a capability call the image refuses BY NAME -- process/spawn's program, argv, output, time and isolation refusals, entropy/draw without getrandom -- each with a `KEXE_TRAP {:kind :capability ...}` line naming the reason."}}}

